      "writtenOn": "2014-08-14T05:33:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "battery_is_present() is only defined for boards with battery, so I couldn\u0027t just guard this with CONFIG_USB_POWER_DELIVERY. I looked for config flag for battery, but it seemed there is no a single config flag to indicate \"there\u0027s a battery on this board\", so I added a new flag for this. I can change this to something like \"#if defined(CONFIG_USB_POWER_DELIVERY) \u0026\u0026 defined(CONFIG_HAS_BATTERY)\" if that looks better to you.\n\nRegarding PD devices without batteries, is there any of those that we would perform flash erase on?",
