      "writtenOn": "2014-08-14T05:33:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "charge_state_v2 gets the information from battery_get_params(). Currently we still need to keep battery_is_present() API for charge_state_v1, and thus I think it\u0027s the most suitable API here. In longer term, once we get rid of charge_state_v1, we can merge battery_is_present into battery_get_params, and then get the information from charge_state_v2.",
